First, we need to find the total number of apples Uncle Franky has. He ordered two boxes, and each box has forty apples. So the total number of apples is 2 boxes * 40 apples/box = 80 apples.

Next, we need to determine how many packs of apples he can make. Each pack contains 8 apples, and he has 80 apples in total. So the number of packs is 80 apples / 8 apples/pack = 10 packs.

\boxed{10}
